    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "PAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS'\nNEW\nDOUBLE\nCLIPPER\nDECKED\nTHE\nCLIPPER\nAMERICA\"\nFirst of The New Fleet\nCLIPPER AMERICA\nPAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS\nThe World's Most Experienced Airline\nTrade Mark. Pan American Airways, Inc.\nCopyright, 1949, Pan American Airways, Inc.",
      "THE NEW\nDOUBLE\nDECKED\nCLIPPER\nCHAMPION OF THE SKYWAYS!\nYou will FLY between\nthe U.S.A. and-\nA new era in air transportation has arrived, borne on the\nwings of Pan American's new double-decked \"America\"-class\nClipper. Biggest commercial landplane in the world, this\nimpressive newcomer is years ahead in design, engineering\nand performance. From the passenger's viewpoint, comfort,\nspeed and security have been combined to a degree un-\ndreamed of only a few months ago.\nBuilt and perfected by the same manufacturer who pro-\nduced the war-time B-17 and B-29 bombers, the \"America\"-\nclass Clipper is the commercial version of the non-stop\nworld-girding B-50 Superfort. This double-decked, luxury\nairliner will turn previously tiresome inter-continental jour-\nneys into brief flights of utmost comfort and convenience.\nThe vast Atlantic and Pacific oceans will now be spanned in\nmany hours less than ever before... the long flight between\nthe United States and Rio de Janeiro or Buenos Aires will\nbe cut by as much as half a day.\nIn 1949 alone, twenty of the \"America\"-class Clippers\nwill be carrying the flag of the United States, establishing\nnew records for speed and distance all over the world.\nPan American's Round-the-World Route together with\nthe network that serves 73 countries and colonies will come\nto know the majestic sight of these unrivalled double-decked\nchampions of the skyways of tomorrow.\nA9BOIN\n• • HAWAII, IN 9 HOURS\n• •• EUROPE, IN 12 HOURS\n••• RIO DE JANEIRO,\nIN 18 HOURS",
      "PAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS\nTHE WORLD'S MOST EXPERIENCED AIRLINE\nOnly Giant Pan American Clippers fly to all six continents,\nNorth America-South America-Europe-Africa-Asia-Australia.\nNew business will follow when you give your cargoes\nwings via CLIPPER CARGO.\nFor information and reservations\nsee your own travel agent\nor your nearest Pan American World Airways Office\nBOSTON 17, MASS....\n....Statler Hotel.......\n.Liberty 2-3720\nBRONX 59, N. Y...\n...910 East 163 St...\nLudlow 9-7640\nBROOKLYN 2, N. Y.....\n..St. George Hotel, 51 Clark St.....\n...Stillwell 6-0600\nCHICAGO 1, ILL...\n.300 N. Michigan Avenue...\nDearborn 2-4900\nCLEVELAND 14, OHIO....Rm. 512, Union Commerce Bldg..........Tower 1-2520\nDETROIT 26, MICH.....\n...Room 53, Penobscot Bldg........ Woodward 2-9435\nHOLLYWOOD 28, CAL....\n...Hollywood Roosevelt Hotel\n....Hillside 1141\nHOUSTON 2, TEXAS..\nMellie Esperson Bldg..\nBeacon 3-9331\nLAREDO, TEXAS...\nHamiiton Hotel..\n..Laredo 2612\nLOS ANGELES 14, CAL..\n506 West Sixth St...\n...Michigan 2121\nMIAMI 32, FLA..\n.2 Biscayne Blyd..\n88-1661\nMIAMI BEACH, FLA....\n.....1632 Collins Ave..\n.....88-1661\nMINNEAPOLIS 2, MINN.\n200 Rand Tower\nLincoln 0617\nNEW ORLEANS 12, LA.\n.....148 Carondelet St.\n....Canal 6391\nNEW YORK 17, N. Y.\n80 East 42 St.....\nSrillwell 6-0600\nNEW YORK 5, N. Y...\n....100 Broadway....\n...Stillwell 6-0600\nNEW YORK 20, N. Y.\n620 Fifth Avenue.\n...Stillwell 6-0600\nRockefeller Center Promenade\nPHILADELPHIA 3, PA..\n...1636 Walnut St...\nPORTLAND, OREGON......Rm. 209, American Bank Bldg..\nST. LOUIS 1, MISSOURI.\n818 Olive St.\nSAN DIEGO, CALIF\n..U. S. Grant Hotel.\nSAN FRANCISCO 8, CAL.\n.222 Stockton St....\nSEATTLE 1, WASH...\n1302 Fourth Avenue...\nWASHINGTON 6, D.C.....\n......1109 Connecticut Ave.\n.Kingsley 5-5100\nBroadway 6677\nMain 1620\n....Main 6133\nGarfield 1-3075\n....Seneca 2121\nRepublic 5700\nPAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS SYSTEM"
